  "prompt": "Which products have one of the two highest unit costs in their category? Products that tie on unit cost share a place, and the next lower cost takes the next place number with no gap, so a category can have more than two such products. Return four columns, in this order: category_id, product_id, unit_cost_eur and cost_place, the product's place in its category, 1 or 2. Return one row for each such product. Any row order is fine.",
